        "content": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint A[1000][1000];\ntypedef long long ll;\nll ps[1010][1010];\n\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\n  for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n      ps[i][j] = (ll)A[i - 1][j - 1] + ps[i - 1][j] + ps[i][j - 1] - ps[i - 1][j - 1];\n    }\n  }\n\n  unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\n  ll ans = 0;\n  for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++)\n    for (int l = j; l <= n; l++) {\n      h.clear();\n      h[0] = 1;\n      for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n        // This is the cumulative sum through row i for columns j..l.\n        // Reading it directly avoids a loop-carried running-sum dependency.\n        ll s = ps[i][l] - ps[i][j - 1];\n        ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\n        h[s]++;\n      }\n    }\n  return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  int k, m, n;\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\n  memset(A, 0, sizeof A);\n  memset(ps, 0, sizeof ps);\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\n      cin >> A[i][j];\n\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\n  return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/main.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Using a 2D prefix table lets each row's cumulative sum for a column stripe be read directly, removing the loop-carried running-sum recurrence while preserving the sequential histogram updates needed for correctness. This may shorten the scan's dependency chain, though the hash-map work remains scalar.",
